<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 http://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <parent>
        <artifactId>forge</artifactId>
        <groupId>forge</groupId>
        <version>${revision}</version>
    </parent>

    <artifactId>forge-gui-teavm</artifactId>
    <packaging>jar</packaging>
    <name>Forge TeaVM Web</name>

    <!--
      gdx-teavm web backend integration module.
      ==========================================
      This module targets an HTML5/WebGL deployment of the Forge mobile UI using
      the gdx-teavm backend (https://github.com/xpenatan/gdx-teavm).

      KEY DESIGN PRINCIPLE: ALL changes live within this module.  No other module
      is modified.  Incompatible third-party libraries are handled by:
        1. Excluding the offending JAR from this module's transitive classpath.
        2. Providing a no-op stub in src/main/java/ under the original package name.
      Maven places the current module's compiled classes before transitive
      dependency JARs, so the stubs shadow the real classes for both javac and
      the TeaVM compilation classpath.

      WHY gdx-teavm OVER gdx-backend-gwt (the existing forge-gui-html):
        - TeaVM compiles from bytecode (.class files), not Java source.  No
          source JARs are needed – the biggest obstacle for GWT.
        - gdx-teavm is actively maintained (as of 2025); gdx-backend-gwt has
          been effectively abandoned since LibGDX 1.9.x.
        - TeaVM emulates a wider subset of the Java standard library than GWT.

      IMPLEMENTATION PLAN (ordered steps to get the home screen loading)
      ===================================================================

      Step 1 – LibGDX version alignment  [WITHIN this module only]
        gdx-teavm 1.5.3 requires LibGDX 1.14.0.  The project currently uses
        1.13.5.  This module explicitly declares gdx 1.14.0; Maven's
        "nearest-wins" dependency resolution picks it for this module's
        classpath without touching any other module's POM.
        Verify: `mvn -pl forge-gui-teavm dependency:tree | grep gdx`

      Step 2 – Stub replacements for incompatible libraries  [WITHIN this module]
        The following libraries are excluded from forge-gui-teavm's transitive
        classpath and replaced by no-op stubs in src/main/java/:
          a) org.jupnp (UPnP networking) → stubs/org/jupnp/
             Used by: IDeviceAdapter.getUpnpPlatformService(), FServerManager
             Impact: Multiplayer UPnP port-mapping is disabled; direct-IP play
                     still works and is unaffected.
          b) io.sentry (crash reporting) → stubs/io/sentry/ and io/sentry/protocol/
             Used by: Forge.java, BugReporter, SaveFileData, VCardDisplayArea,
                      LibGDXImageFetcher, HWInfo
             Impact: Crash reports are silently dropped.  A browser-native
                     solution (Sentry browser SDK via @JSBody) can be added later.

      Step 3 – java.nio.file  [WITHIN this module, but requires further work]
        Forge.java (Files.exists) and FSkinFont.java (Files.newInputStream) use
        java.nio.file.  TeaVM's JS-mode emulation:
          - Files.exists → returns false (safe: Forge uses it as a feature flag
            for adventure textures; false is a harmless fallback).
          - Files.newInputStream → throws UnsupportedOperationException at runtime.
        The FSkinFont path is the critical one (translation file loading).
        Fix within this module: add a TeaVM ClassHolderTransformer in
        BuildForgeTeaVM.java that replaces the Files.newInputStream call in
        FSkinFont.class with an empty InputStream, effectively disabling
        i18n translation loading on the web target.

      Step 4 – TeaVM compilation  [WITHIN this module]
        Run: `mvn -pl forge-gui-teavm -Pteavm package`
        The TeaCompiler compiles TeaVMLauncher and all reachable classes to JS.
        Expected first-pass errors to address iteratively:
          - Missing class references in TeaVM's class library (add more stubs
            or exclude more jars as needed).
          - Reflection usage (Class.forName with dynamic strings) in NewGameMenu,
            LoadGameMenu, OnlineMenu, SaveFileData: add those classes to the
            TeaVM compiler's preserved-class list in BuildForgeTeaVM.java.
          - Box2D: exclude gdx-box2d native lib (adventure mode is out of scope).

      Step 5 – Smoke test  [WITHIN this module]
        After step 4 produces output in target/dist/webapp/:
          `mvn -pl forge-gui-teavm -Pteavm integration-test`
        Runs HomeScreenLoadTest.java (Playwright Java) which:
          a) Starts an in-process HTTP server serving target/dist/webapp/.
          b) Opens headless Chromium and navigates to the page.
          c) Polls window.__forgeReady (set by TeaVMLauncher once
             Forge.afterDBloaded == true) up to 90 s.
          d) Fails if any uncaught JS exception appears in the console.

      Step 6 – CI integration  [workflow files only]
        Add a GitHub Actions job that:
          1. Installs Playwright browsers: `mvn exec:java ... playwright install chromium`
          2. Runs steps 4 + 5.
          3. Uploads target/dist/webapp/ as a GitHub Pages artifact.
    -->

    <properties>
        <gdx.teavm.version>1.5.3</gdx.teavm.version>
        <!--
          Explicitly declare LibGDX 1.14.0 here.  gdx-teavm 1.5.3 requires this
          version.  forge-gui-mobile uses 1.13.5; Maven's nearest-wins rule means
          this declaration (depth 1) beats the 1.13.5 declaration (depth 2) for
          this module's effective classpath only.  No other module is affected.
        -->
        <gdx.version>1.14.0</gdx.version>
        <playwright.version>1.52.0</playwright.version>
    </properties>

    <dependencies>
        <!-- Forge mobile UI (the shared LibGDX-based front-end) -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>forge</groupId>
            <artifactId>forge-gui-mobile</artifactId>
            <version>${project.version}</version>
            <exclusions>
                <!--
                  Exclude org.jupnp: replaced by no-op stubs in
                  src/main/java/org/jupnp/.
                  UPnP is unused in the browser; the stub UpnpServiceConfiguration
                  interface satisfies all compile-time type references without
                  pulling in the ~5 MB jupnp jar.
                -->
                <exclusion>
                    <groupId>org.jupnp</groupId>
                    <artifactId>org.jupnp</artifactId>
                </exclusion>
                <exclusion>
                    <groupId>org.jupnp</groupId>
                    <artifactId>org.jupnp.support</artifactId>
                </exclusion>
                <!--
                  Exclude io.sentry: replaced by no-op stubs in
                  src/main/java/io/sentry/.
                  Sentry error reporting is silently disabled on the web target.
                -->
                <exclusion>
                    <groupId>io.sentry</groupId>
                    <artifactId>*</artifactId>
                </exclusion>
            </exclusions>
        </dependency>

        <!-- LibGDX core – explicitly declared to enforce 1.14.0 over 1.13.5 -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>com.badlogicgames.gdx</groupId>
            <artifactId>gdx</artifactId>
            <version>${gdx.version}</version>
        </dependency>

        <!--
          gdx-teavm web backend.
          Contains:
            - WebApplication / WebApplicationConfiguration (compiled to JS)
            - TeaCompiler / WebBackend (build-time JVM tool)
            - Pre-built gdx.wasm.js (LibGDX native code via Emscripten)
        -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>com.github.xpenatan.gdx-teavm</groupId>
            <artifactId>backend-web</artifactId>
            <version>${gdx.teavm.version}</version>
        </dependency>

        <!--
          FreeType font rendering for TeaVM.
          Forge uses gdx-freetype for FSkinFont; this extension ships the
          Emscripten-compiled FreeType Wasm module for the browser.
        -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>com.github.xpenatan.gdx-teavm</groupId>
            <artifactId>gdx-freetype-teavm</artifactId>
            <version>${gdx.teavm.version}</version>
        </dependency>

        <!--
          Playwright Java – headless browser automation for HomeScreenLoadTest.
          Scope: test only; not included in the TeaVM compilation output.

          Before running integration tests, install browsers with:
            mvn exec:java \
              -Dexec.mainClass="com.microsoft.playwright.CLI" \
              -Dexec.args="install chromium" \
              -pl forge-gui-teavm
        -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>com.microsoft.playwright</groupId>
            <artifactId>playwright</artifactId>
            <version>${playwright.version}</version>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>

        <!-- TestNG – consistent with the existing forge-gui-desktop test suite -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.testng</groupId>
            <artifactId>testng</artifactId>
            <version>7.10.2</version>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>
    </dependencies>

    <build>
        <plugins>
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
                <artifactId>maven-compiler-plugin</artifactId>
                <!--
                  Both BuildForgeTeaVM (build-time driver) and TeaVMLauncher
                  (browser-side entry point) live in the same source tree and
                  are compiled together by javac.  The TeaCompiler then
                  cross-compiles TeaVMLauncher from the resulting bytecode.
                -->
            </plugin>

            <!--
              Skip surefire during the normal test phase; integration tests
              require the TeaVM build output and are run separately with
              -Pteavm integration-test.
            -->
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
                <artifactId>maven-surefire-plugin</artifactId>
                <configuration>
                    <excludedGroups>teavm-smoke</excludedGroups>
                </configuration>
            </plugin>
        </plugins>
    </build>

    <!--
      -Pteavm: compile the TeaVM JS output + run the smoke test.

      Usage:
        mvn -pl forge-gui-teavm -Pteavm package           # JS build only
        mvn -pl forge-gui-teavm -Pteavm integration-test  # JS build + smoke test

      Prerequisites:
        1. Run `mvn install -DskipTests` from the project root first to put all
           Forge JARs in the local Maven repo.
        2. Playwright browsers must be installed (one-time):
             mvn exec:java -Dexec.mainClass="com.microsoft.playwright.CLI" \
                           -Dexec.args="install chromium" \
                           -pl forge-gui-teavm
    -->
    <profiles>
        <profile>
            <id>teavm</id>
            <build>
                <plugins>
                    <!--
                      Run the build-time TeaCompiler driver (BuildForgeTeaVM)
                      during the package phase to produce JS from bytecode.

                      Output: target/dist/webapp/
                              ├── index.html
                              ├── forge.js        (transpiled game code)
                              ├── gdx.wasm.js     (LibGDX native Wasm via Emscripten)
                              └── assets/         (game resources)
                    -->
                    <plugin>
                        <groupId>org.codehaus.mojo</groupId>
                        <artifactId>exec-maven-plugin</artifactId>
                        <version>3.3.0</version>
                        <executions>
                            <execution>
                                <id>build-teavm</id>
                                <phase>package</phase>
                                <goals>
                                    <goal>java</goal>
                                </goals>
                                <configuration>
                                    <mainClass>forge.teavm.BuildForgeTeaVM</mainClass>
                                    <includeProjectDependencies>true</includeProjectDependencies>
                                    <includePluginDependencies>false</includePluginDependencies>
                                    <!--
                                      Run BuildForgeTeaVM with the module directory as the working
                                      directory so that relative paths (assetsDir, outputDir) are
                                      resolved correctly regardless of whether Maven is invoked from
                                      the project root or the module directory.
                                    -->
                                    <workingDirectory>${project.basedir}</workingDirectory>
                                    <systemProperties>
                                        <!--
                                          Pass the module's build directory so BuildForgeTeaVM can
                                          write to forge-gui-teavm/target/dist rather than to the
                                          root project's target directory.
                                        -->
                                        <systemProperty>
                                            <key>forge.buildDir</key>
                                            <value>${project.build.directory}</value>
                                        </systemProperty>
                                    </systemProperties>
                                </configuration>
                            </execution>
                        </executions>
                    </plugin>

                    <!--
                      Run HomeScreenLoadTest during integration-test phase.
                      This requires Playwright browsers to be installed and the
                      TeaVM build output to be present at target/dist/webapp/.
                    -->
                    <plugin>
                        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
                        <artifactId>maven-failsafe-plugin</artifactId>
                        <version>3.1.2</version>
                        <configuration>
                            <includes>
                                <include>**/*LoadTest.java</include>
                            </includes>
                            <groups>teavm-smoke</groups>
                            <!--
                              Run integration tests with the module directory as
                              the working directory so HomeScreenLoadTest finds
                              target/dist/webapp/ correctly regardless of whether
                              Maven is invoked from the root or the module.
                            -->
                            <workingDirectory>${project.basedir}</workingDirectory>
                        </configuration>
                        <executions>
                            <execution>
                                <goals>
                                    <goal>integration-test</goal>
                                    <goal>verify</goal>
                                </goals>
                            </execution>
                        </executions>
                    </plugin>
                </plugins>
            </build>
        </profile>
    </profiles>
</project>
